# Launch-readiness audit, SEC-014.
#
# `frame-ancestors` is SPEC-IGNORED in a <meta> CSP, so clickjacking
# protection has to arrive as a real response header - which matters
# because ~19 destructive actions sit behind a confirm sheet that a
# framing attacker could bait a click onto.
#
# This file is the Cloudflare Pages format, and Cloudflare Pages has been
# the host since 2026-09-16: these headers are what production sends. (The
# previous host, GitHub Pages, could not send headers at all, which is why
# frame-guard.js and the meta CSP exist as backstops.) docs/deploy/HEADERS.md
# is the superseded plan from that era; verify with `curl -sI` on the site.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), usb=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
